      <h2>Typical ranges</h2>
      <table><thead><tr><th>Kitchen</th><th>Furniture</th><th>With worktops &amp; appliances</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Galley or small L-shape</td><td>[£X–£X]</td><td>[£X–£X]</td></tr><tr><td>Island kitchen, family home</td><td>[£X–£X]</td><td>[£X–£X]</td></tr><tr><td>Large open-plan with pantry and utility</td><td>[£X–£X]</td><td>[£X–£X]</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <h2>What moves the number</h2>
      <p>Six things move the number, roughly in this order: the SieMatic collection and front material (a lacquer is one price, a smoked-oak veneer or metal front another); the worktop, where quartz, porcelain and natural stone sit a long way apart; the appliance brand — Siemens, Miele or Gaggenau changes the total by more than the cabinetry does; the island and any tall-unit wall, which carry most of the cost per metre; bespoke interior fittings and lighting; and the installation itself, which depends on the room you have rather than the kitchen you want.</p>
      <h2>What is included</h2>
      <p>Every figure includes the design service in full — survey, layouts, 3D visuals and the written specification — plus delivery and the project management that gets it installed. Installation is priced separately, with your installer or one of ours, because every house is different.</p>
      <h2>There is no design fee</h2>
      <p>The appointment, survey, drawings and specification are free. The price you are quoted is for the products and, if you want it, installation.</p>
